TempData must be used in the following scenarios:

a) Survives Redirects (Post-Redirect-Get Pattern)

TempData persists data across a redirect, unlike ViewData which dies immediately after the current request.

Example:

// POST action &#8211; Create student

[HttpPost]

public IActionResult CreateStudent(Student student)

{

// Save to database

TempData[&#8220;Message&#8221;] = &#8220;Student added successfully!&#8221;;

return RedirectToAction(&#8220;StudentList&#8221;); // Redirect happens

}

// GET action &#8211; After redirect

public IActionResult StudentList()

{

// TempData[&#8220;Message&#8221;] is still available here!

return View();

}

b) Automatically Cleans Up After Being Read

TempData deletes itself after being accessed, preventing memory bloat and eliminating manual cleanup &#8211; unlike Session which requires explicit removal.

Example:

// First Request

public IActionResult Step1()

{

TempData[&#8220;UserChoice&#8221;] = &#8220;Option A&#8221;;

return RedirectToAction(&#8220;Step2&#8221;);

}

// Second Request

public IActionResult Step2()

{

var choice = TempData[&#8220;UserChoice&#8221;]; // Reads the data

return View();

// TempData[&#8220;UserChoice&#8221;] is now automatically deleted!

}

// Third Request

public IActionResult Step3()

{

var choice = TempData[&#8220;UserChoice&#8221;]; // Returns null &#8211; already cleaned up

return View();

}

c) Prevents Duplicate Actions on Page Refresh

By using redirects with TempData, you avoid form resubmission problems when users refresh the page.

Example:

// Without TempData (Bad Practice)

[HttpPost]

public IActionResult DeleteStudent(int id)

{

// Delete student

ViewData[&#8220;Status&#8221;] = &#8220;Deleted!&#8221;;

return View(&#8220;Confirmation&#8221;); // No redirect

// Problem: Refreshing page will delete again!

}

// With TempData (Best Practice)

[HttpPost]

public IActionResult DeleteStudent(int id)

{

// Delete student

TempData[&#8220;Status&#8221;] = &#8220;Student deleted successfully!&#8221;;

return RedirectToAction(&#8220;Index&#8221;); // Redirect to safe page

// Refreshing page only reloads the list, no re-deletion

}

public IActionResult Index()

{

// Message displays once, then disappears

return View();

}

